WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.499 --> 00:00:05.549
The nature of faith, the power of grief, and
how to kill a monster you can't even see.

00:00:05.549 --> 00:00:11.190
"Bird Box Barcelona" raises some big questions,
and its ending opens up plenty of possibilities

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:12.630
for future sequels.

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:14.722
Warning - spoilers ahead.

00:00:14.722 --> 00:00:19.150
Before getting into the events of "Bird Box
Barcelona," it makes sense to do a recap of

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:23.055
some details from the first film that are
crucial to the new story.

00:00:23.055 --> 00:00:27.350
Staying alive is immensely challenging in
the world of "Bird Box;" survivors are forced

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:31.110
to blindly traverse areas to avoid seeing
the creatures.

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:36.220
Those who are lured into looking at the creatures
have one of two fates: either they kill themselves

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:40.770
or they're manipulated into becoming a Seer
to carry out the creatures' requests.

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:45.050
Even if survivors manage to keep their blindfolds
on, the creatures can mimic the voices of

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:50.575
lost loved ones or anyone close to their victims
to try and convince them to take their blindfolds off.

00:00:50.575 --> 00:00:55.895
In "Barcelona," the creatures' power is even
deadlier, but they face even savvier survivors.

00:00:55.895 --> 00:01:00.380
There's a greater focus on putting blindfolds
on animals in "Barcelona" since the creatures

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:05.260
can affect them, too, and there are new kinds
of blinders the survivors use, like Sebastián's

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:06.540
blacked-out goggles.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:11.200
More new survival tactics utilize sounds and
dogs to alert groups of the creatures' presence.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:16.180
However, not even the best survivors can be
prepared for the arrival of a Seer, a faction

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:21.079
that's also much craftier and deadlier than
we see in the original "Bird Box."

00:01:21.079 --> 00:01:24.860
Sebastián is a dedicated Seer at the start
of "Bird Box Barcelona."

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:30.354
He's shown to be capable of devastating and
unpredictable actions against unsuspecting survivors.

00:01:30.354 --> 00:01:35.409
He has no place for mercy in his mission to
"save people" and is especially dangerous

00:01:35.409 --> 00:01:37.322
to a new group he comes across.

00:01:37.322 --> 00:01:41.450
As the survivors try to make it to a possible
safe haven up in the mountains, Sebastián

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:43.310
works toward sabotaging them.

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:47.799
He lies to them about everything and lets
the group's dogs loose to deprive them of

00:01:47.799 --> 00:01:49.219
their canine guides.

00:01:49.219 --> 00:01:54.399
However, he's not able to stay under the radar
for long, as English survivor Claire is able

00:01:54.399 --> 00:01:56.430
to uncover the truth about him.

00:01:56.430 --> 00:02:00.689
But as Sebastián travels with the group,
he begins to question his purpose and whether

00:02:00.689 --> 00:02:03.116
his actions are really "saving" people.

00:02:03.116 --> 00:02:07.770
Soon, he's unable to ignore the carnage around
him and begins to have a change of heart as

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:10.925
he remembers what life was like before becoming
a Seer.

00:02:10.925 --> 00:02:15.760
His time with Claire and a young German girl
named Sofia starts to clear his mind of the

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:17.203
creatures' control over him.

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:21.500
It's why Sebastián eventually breaks from
his Seer control and decides to help Claire

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:26.470
and Sofia reach safety just as his leader
who killed his daughter years prior confronts

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:27.970
the survivors.

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:32.700
Once Sebastián rejects his status as a Seer,
he does everything in his power to get Claire

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.376
and Sofia to the aerial tramway that will
take them to the supposed safe haven in the mountains.

00:02:37.376 --> 00:02:41.709
However, Father Esteban and his fellow Seers
are hot on their tail.

00:02:41.709 --> 00:02:47.095
It ultimately leads Sebastián to send Claire
and Sofia forward so he can keep the Seers at bay.

00:02:47.095 --> 00:02:52.341
While Sebastián is able to create a blockade
to the tramway by making a car explode, it's

00:02:52.341 --> 00:02:56.860
not enough to keep the power of the creatures
and Esteban from manipulating him.

00:02:56.860 --> 00:03:01.730
Esteban and a hallucination of Anna continue
to try and restore Sebastián's faith, but

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:05.580
Sebastián remains firm and no longer believes
that God would want this.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.000
"Why did you abandon us?"

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:11.300
"Because deep down I always knew that you
killed her."

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:16.360
However, this doesn't stop Esteban, now masquerading
as the hallucination of Anna, from miraculously

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:19.310
walking over the flaming car toward Sebastián.

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:23.810
To prove his independence from the creatures,
Sebastián charges Anna and ends up stabbing

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:25.599
Esteban through the gut.

00:03:25.599 --> 00:03:30.837
Unfortunately, Esteban pulls Sebastián onto
the metal rod as well which punctures his torso.

00:03:30.837 --> 00:03:34.383
Sebastián decides to not fight back to keep
Esteban trapped.

00:03:34.383 --> 00:03:37.934
They both end up dying as a result of Sebastián's
sacrifice.

00:03:37.934 --> 00:03:42.337
While it's sad to see the reformed Seer fall,
his wishes to reunite with his family and

00:03:42.337 --> 00:03:44.750
finally do the right thing are fulfilled.

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:49.410
While Sebastián makes his sacrifice, Claire
and Sofia try to make their escape.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:54.030
They nearly meet a quick death from the tower
falling apart and seem stuck with no way to

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:56.010
power the lift from their location.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:04:00.200
Claire realizes that she has to alert the
people on the other side that they need help

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:04.010
by ringing a bell, but the sound draws the
attention of one of the creatures.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:08.900
When it arrives, it torments Claire with maddening
voices and nearly kills Sofia by luring her

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:11.579
toward the edge of the tower with her mother's
voice.

00:04:11.579 --> 00:04:16.987
Thankfully, Claire keeps her head, saves Sofia,
and gets both of them onto the moving tram safely.

00:04:16.987 --> 00:04:20.970
When Claire and Sofia arrive at the castle,
they find a sanctuary that's very similar

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:23.750
to the one that Malorie finds at the end of
the first film.

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:29.123
In the safe haven, Sofia has a tearful reunion
with her mother, and Claire starts to receive treatment.

00:04:29.123 --> 00:04:33.630
While talking to a doctor about Sebastián
and the other Seers, Claire realizes that

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:37.280
the creatures could be tapping into people's
grief and trauma to control them.

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:38.470
"They can be reached, you know.

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:40.443
They're still in there…somewhere."

00:04:40.443 --> 00:04:44.160
It's at this point that they discover that
the facility is running tests on a Seer they

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:47.210
captured to find a cure, but that's not all
that's here.

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:51.810
The survivors also have a creature locked
in a containment room and are using it for

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:55.566
tests, leaving a foreboding air over the finale
of the movie.

00:04:55.566 --> 00:05:01.020
One of the biggest themes of "Bird Box Barcelona"
is how faith and trauma are used as destructive

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:04.230
tools, both by the creatures, Esteban, and
his followers.

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:08.330
Sebastián is originally led to believe that
the creatures are "angels" sent by God to

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:10.270
guide him in his path to save humanity.

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:15.837
But his eyes are opened and he sees that their
only desire is to orchestrate cruel and painful deaths.

00:05:15.837 --> 00:05:21.120
A big reason that Sebastián and even Esteban
are turned into Seers is because of the distinct

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.934
grief and emptiness they share.

00:05:22.934 --> 00:05:27.050
Esteban has lost his faith by the time he
becomes a Seer and is desperate to believe

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:30.830
again, while Sebastián is suffering from
immense grief stemming from the loss of his

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:32.786
family, especially Anna.

00:05:32.786 --> 00:05:37.380
That's why she is an influential, spiritual
guide for Sebastián and why she becomes one

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:40.060
of the keys to the creatures' control over
him.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:44.270
Claire even has a conversation with a sanctuary
doctor highlighting how the creatures use

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:47.223
grief and emotion to target vulnerable people.

00:05:47.223 --> 00:05:51.450
This depiction of the creatures' power touches
on how faith can be manipulated to justify

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:56.040
terrible acts and convince suffering people
to take dangerous paths.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:59.979
Sebastián breaks through the destructive
sense of faith instilled by the creatures,

00:05:59.979 --> 00:06:03.010
and it's ultimately what makes him capable
of redemption.

00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:07.710
While Sebastián's redemption symbolizes a
thematic change of heart for the character,

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:10.682
it also represents a major turning point for
the franchise.

00:06:10.682 --> 00:06:13.462
His story shows that the Seers can be cured.

00:06:13.462 --> 00:06:18.980
For the first time, we see that a Seer can
actually defy the creatures' power and act independently.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:23.080
Claire tells Sebastián's story to the people
of the sanctuary, and it means that others

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:25.020
may find ways to stop the Seers.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:28.940
However, Claire is far from the first to know
that Seers can be cured.

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:32.599
In the final scene, it's revealed that this
new group of survivors is trying to find a

00:06:32.599 --> 00:06:36.500
way to cure Seers by testing the blood of
one who's been captured.

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:40.880
The tests aren't just for curing Seers, though,
as the ending also implies that scientists

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:43.009
are looking for a way to fight the creatures.

00:06:43.009 --> 00:06:47.479
The survivors are also exposing animal test
subjects to the captured creature in the hopes

00:06:47.479 --> 00:06:50.253
of finding an antidote of sorts to their powers.

00:06:50.253 --> 00:06:54.940
Sebastián saved two people, but perhaps this
research will make humans immune to the monster's

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:57.695
power and turn the tables against them.

00:06:57.695 --> 00:07:02.190
Although Netflix has been pretty quiet about
"Bird Box Barcelona" leading up to its release,

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:07.880
there has been some discussion by lead star
Mario Casas about his character, Sebastián.

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:12.520
In an interview with MovieWeb, Casas not only
discussed his genuine love for the "Bird Box"

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:17.660
franchise, but also how Sebastián is depicted
as a complex and emotionally compelling character.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:18.445
He said,

00:07:18.445 --> 00:07:22.720
"I think it was important to have a complex
character who should also have a very deep

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:26.069
emotional side, and I think it's something
that hooks the audience.

00:07:26.069 --> 00:07:30.449
I like when a character is not always a hero,
and he has many more layers, and he has a

00:07:30.449 --> 00:07:32.629
dark side, and there's ambiguity."

00:07:32.629 --> 00:07:37.095
This is a perfect way to describe Sebastián's
character and his emotional story arc.

00:07:37.095 --> 00:07:41.730
Casas also went on to describe his views of
the creatures that tie to some of the realizations

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:44.253
made by Claire later in the film, revealing,

00:07:44.253 --> 00:07:48.190
"Well, I would say that it has a lot more
to do about trauma and how these characters

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:49.360
have this lack of humanity.

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:54.949
I was thinking more of these creatures as
feelings of fear, stress, loss, sorrow."

00:07:54.949 --> 00:07:58.940
His analysis of the creatures as being more
emotional and mental entities rather than

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:04.280
physical ones fits perfectly into their depiction
in the world of "Bird Box" and how they torment

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:05.417
their victims.

00:08:05.417 --> 00:08:12.860
"Then they take form based on us: our fears,
our grief, our pain…"

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:17.990
The ending of "Bird Box Barcelona" leaves
the future of the franchise at an interesting crossroads.

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:22.139
There seems to be more story to tell with
these Barcelona survivors; a sequel could

00:08:22.139 --> 00:08:26.240
see Claire and other members of the sanctuary
in a dangerous new fight for their lives if

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:28.199
the contained creature breaks out.

00:08:28.199 --> 00:08:33.731
Or Claire could lead a group to another sanctuary
and continue to research how to defeat the creatures.

00:08:33.731 --> 00:08:37.830
Of course, the "Bird Box" series has already
expressed interest in taking its formula around

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:41.340
the world, so we could see another entry set
in a different country.

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:45.977
It would let us see how other survivors in
a different setting are coping with this dark new reality.

00:08:45.977 --> 00:08:50.220
It could also lead to more reveals about the
creatures and survivors, and maybe that story

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:53.910
could build toward a larger world that would
see different characters come together to

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:55.690
take out the creatures for good.

00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:58.230
The possibilities are endless.

00:08:58.230 --> 00:09:02.600
With "Bird Box Barcelona" showing that survivors
are testing Seers and looking for a way to

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:06.640
defeat the creatures, future entries could
explain how other countries are approaching

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:08.190
research into the monsters.

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:12.010
It would be interesting to see how other countries
and cultures have been affected by the creatures'

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:14.405
arrival and their destructive abilities.

00:09:14.405 --> 00:09:20.410
With "Barcelona," we got more thematic perspectives
on religion and grief being connected to the creatures.

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:24.010
New international entries could touch on other
aspects of humanity that are being twisted

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:25.580
and manipulated.

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:30.329
While the original "Bird Box" features a star-studded
cast and garnered a lot of attention from

00:09:30.329 --> 00:09:34.080
subscribers when it premiered, it doesn't
seem like we're getting a continuation of

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:35.750
that story any time soon.

00:09:35.750 --> 00:09:40.510
"Bird Box Barcelona" establishes itself as
more of a standalone spin-off set within the

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:45.810
same world, and never directly referencing
or hinting at events or characters from the first film.

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:49.160
But does that mean that we'll never return
to the world of the original?

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:53.510
No, but fans shouldn't expect a true "Bird
Box" sequel for a while.

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:58.120
There haven't been many signs that a more
straightforward "Bird Box 2" is in development,

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:02.952
and the film's ending hints more at a "Barcelona"
sequel rather than another American entry.

00:10:02.952 --> 00:10:06.990
Perhaps if the franchise continues to touch
on different stories and characters from around

00:10:06.990 --> 00:10:11.750
the globe, it can all culminate in a finale
that teams up the survivors to defeat the

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:12.950
creatures for good.

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:17.060
But if a traditional "Bird Box 2" isn't the
next entry in this franchise and the story

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:21.709
continues branching out internationally, it's
likely that a return to the plot and characters

00:10:21.709 --> 00:10:23.689
of the original isn't happening.

